  "analytic_review_groups": [
    "The descended Hopf metric is positive; vertical beta is twice Haar measure, volume is six, and the Gauduchon torsion identities yield mass six plus energy six.",
    "The radial-angular-vertical block matrix and Schur complement give positivity, including the xi=0 endpoint.",
    "The period-four heat kernel has first nonzero eigenvalue one quarter, exponential derivative estimates and the stated Fourier normalization.",
    "The Gaussian-mixture logarithmic Hessian is bounded below by minus one over time.",
    "Parseval differentiation gives minus twice eta squared times (k2*t0-1); the Gaussian error is integrable and the energy grows logarithmically.",
    "The nearest-lattice gradient estimate treats distances below and above one quarter separately.",
    "The completed-square cutoff estimate is uniform, including the zero of the cutoff, where its derivative vanishes.",
    "The exact Q identity retains the mu*(1-mu)-mu squared eta/(1-eta) term.",
    "The chosen epsilon and b scales give eta*b tending to zero and constant endpoint profiles.",
    "Small-time and large-time bounds control the negative defect integral by the stated square-root eta logarithm bound.",
    "Cutoff derivative growth is dominated by exp(-1/(e*eta)); the radial slope estimates remain uniform.",
    "A smooth majorant is compensated on the negative radial interval, and its small first derivative preserves angular positivity.",
    "Energy on a fixed ball diverges logarithmically, while constant endpoints allow the global extension.",
    "The higher-dimensional density is n*(n-1)/6 times (mu+V_x) to power n-3 times the threefold density, with the normalized Fubini-Study factor.",
    "Threefold mass is first localized to x<0; the fibre-mean bound and the separate x>=0 estimate then imply failure of bounded mass in every dimension at least three.",
    "Uniform comparison transfers the witnesses to every smooth positive Hermitian metric on the scalar Hopf manifold.",
    "Fibre averaging descends a plurisubharmonic function; spectral constant four gives the optimal two-thirds bound, and regularization recovers the canonical representative everywhere.",
    "The positive quadratic measure and the full cubic measure differ by a total-variation error bounded by the stated linear, mixed and cubic terms.",
    "Independent random orbital translates and Chebyshev/Markov estimates control cross masses and finitely many test functions, with exact mass normalization.",
    "Compact orbital averaging and finite test nets give uniform convergence and arbitrary base-measure convolution.",
    "Positivity and alpha-wedge-K=0 remove the vertical matrix rows; closedness and fibre Fourier coefficients force the unique pullback intermediate-current limit.",
    "Fixed linear pullbacks have quadratic small-parameter errors; projective dilation produces point concentration, and a dense-test diagonal handles any prescribed parameter sequence.",
    "Finite atomic approximation and orbital convex mixtures realize all Haar lifts, retaining the exact six-times-base-measure normalization and fibre support.",
    "Pluripolar lifting works both ways via fibre submean inequalities, local integrability and upper semicontinuity; the statement retains its outer-measure qualification.",
    "For a general metric the fibre-area weight gives three A_tau, the metric-change remainder tends to zero, and the positive quadratic root enforces the prescribed mass; this does not close general-manifold damping questions."
  ],
